## 7. Security Considerations

- Use minimal Microsoft Graph permissions.
- Keep real credentials, access tokens, and secrets out of GitHub.
- Use synthetic identities and test data in future labs.
- Validate commands before performing identity changes.
- Document security-relevant architecture decisions.

## 8. Lessons Learned

This lab reinforced the importance of establishing a secure IAM development environment before building automation.

I gained practical experience connecting PowerShell to Microsoft Graph and validating access using a limited delegated permission scope.

The lab also established a foundation for treating identity management as an engineering discipline supported by automation, testing, and documentation.

